{"id":"y11-7-l6","label":"7 L6: Sorting Algorithms","steps":[{"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Array Indices","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-do-now","validatorKey":"y11l6_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Array Indices</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">An array is declared <code>ARRAY[1:50] OF STRING</code>.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-do-now-a\">(a) State the index of its first element. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-do-now-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-do-now-b\">(b) State the index of its last element. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-do-now-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"title","label":"Sorting Algorithms","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Sorting Algorithms</h2><p>Year 11, Unit 7 L6</p></div>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-1","label":"Bubble Sort","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Bubble Sort</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A bubble sort repeatedly steps through an array, comparing each pair of neighbours and swapping them if they are the wrong way round.</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Each full pass compares position 1 with 2, then 2 with 3, and so on to the end.</li><li>The largest unsorted value \"bubbles\" to the end of the array on every pass.</li><li>A Swap flag, just like the Found flag from linear search, records whether anything changed this pass.</li><li>If a whole pass finishes with no swaps, the array is already sorted and the algorithm can stop early.</li></ul>"},{"id":"teacher-talk-1-trace","label":"Trace a Bubble Sort","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y11l6-stepper-1","stepperKey":"bubble_sort_trace","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Trace a Bubble Sort</h2><div id=\"y11l6-stepper-1\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-1","label":"Debug a Bubble Sort","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-activity-1","validatorKey":"y11l6_activity_1","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Debug a Bubble Sort</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This algorithm is intended to sort 200 names in ascending order, using a bubble sort. The last names and first names are stored in separate columns of a 2D array, with last names in column 1. It has five errors.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;// The array Names[] has already been declared as</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;// ARRAY[1:200, 1:2] OF STRING and it is already populated</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Row : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Temp1 : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Temp2 : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Swap : BOOLEAN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;Swap &lt;- FALSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">08&nbsp;&nbsp;WHILE NOT Swap DO</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">09&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Swap &lt;- FALSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">10&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Row &lt;- 2 TO 199</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">11&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Names[Row, 1] &gt; Names[Row + 1, 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">12&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">13&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Temp1 &lt;- Names[Row, 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">14&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Temp2 &lt;- Names[Row, 2]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">15&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Row, 1] &lt;- Names[Row + 1, 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">16&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Row, 1] &lt;- Names[Row + 1, 2]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">17&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Row + 1, 1] &lt;- Temp1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">18&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Row + 1, 2] &lt;- Temp2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">19&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Swap &lt;- FALSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">20&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">21&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Column</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">22&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDWHILE</div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-1-a\">(a) Row is used as a numeric loop counter and array index, so line 03 declares the wrong data type. Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-1-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-1-a\" aria-label=\"Activity 1 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-1-b\">(b) Line 09 must assume the array is sorted at the start of each pass, or the loop can never detect a fully-sorted array. Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-1-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-1-b\" aria-label=\"Activity 1 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-1-c\">(c) Line 10 starts the loop one position too late, so the first two names are never compared. Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-1-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-1-c\" aria-label=\"Activity 1 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-1-d\">(d) Line 16 should update the first name (column 2), but instead overwrites the last name (column 1) that line 15 just set. Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-1-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-1-d\" aria-label=\"Activity 1 part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-1-e\">(e) Line 21 must close the FOR loop using its own loop variable, not one that is never declared. Write the corrected line. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-1-e\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-1-e\" aria-label=\"Activity 1 part e\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-activity-1-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 5 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-activity-1-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, February/March 2026 Paper 22, Question 5(a)</p></div>"},{"id":"activity-2","label":"Why Might It Still Sort Wrongly?","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-activity-2","validatorKey":"y11l6_activity_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Why Might It Still Sort Wrongly?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Even with all five corrections applied, the algorithm can still fail to sort the names accurately.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-2-a\">(a) Describe a possible problem with the algorithm that could mean the names are not sorted accurately. [2]</label><textarea id=\"y11l6-activity-2-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"activity-2-a\" aria-label=\"Activity 2 part a\" spellcheck=\"false\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-activity-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-activity-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478, February/March 2026 Paper 22, Question 5(c)</p></div>"},{"id":"activity-3","label":"Practice: Trace a Bubble Sort","type":"embedded-app","appId":"trace-table-practice","embedContainerId":"y11l6-embed-3","embedQuery":"support=1","embedView":"practice","algorithm":{"title":"Bubble Sort","context":"The array numbers holds [6, 1, 4].","code":["numbers = [6, 1, 4]","swapped = True","while swapped:","    swapped = False","    for i in range(0, 2):","        if numbers[i] > numbers[i + 1]:","            temp = numbers[i]","            numbers[i] = numbers[i + 1]","            numbers[i + 1] = temp","            swapped = True","print(numbers)"],"cols":["Line","i","numbers[0]","numbers[1]","numbers[2]","swapped","Output"],"answers":[{"Line":"4","i":"","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"False","Output":""},{"Line":"5","i":"0","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"9","i":"","numbers[0]":"1","numbers[1]":"6","numbers[2]":"4","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"10","i":"","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"True","Output":""},{"Line":"5","i":"1","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"9","i":"","numbers[0]":"1","numbers[1]":"4","numbers[2]":"6","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"10","i":"","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"True","Output":""},{"Line":"4","i":"","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"False","Output":""},{"Line":"5","i":"0","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"5","i":"1","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"","Output":""},{"Line":"11","i":"","numbers[0]":"","numbers[1]":"","numbers[2]":"","swapped":"","Output":"[1, 4, 6]"}]},"content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Practice: Trace a Bubble Sort</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Complete the trace table. Record a row whenever i, an element of numbers, swapped or the output changes.</p><div id=\"y11l6-embed-3\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-4","label":"Complete a Real Bubble Sort","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-activity-4","validatorKey":"y11l6_activity_4","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Complete a Real Bubble Sort</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This algorithm uses a bubble sort to sort the array Names[50]. Complete the four blanks.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Last &lt;- <em>(a)</em></div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">REPEAT</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Swap &lt;- <em>(b)</em></div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR <em>(c)</em> &lt;- 1 TO Last - 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Names[Index] &gt; Names[Index + 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Temp &lt;- Names[Index]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Index] &lt;- Names[Index + 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Names[Index + 1] &lt;- Temp</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Swap &lt;- TRUE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Index</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;Last &lt;- Last - 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">UNTIL <em>(d)</em> Swap OR Last = 1</div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-4-a\">(a) Last &lt;- .................. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-4-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-4-a\" aria-label=\"Activity 4 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-4-b\">(b) Swap &lt;- .................. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-4-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-4-b\" aria-label=\"Activity 4 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-4-c\">(c) FOR .................. &lt;- 1 TO Last - 1 [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-4-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-4-c\" aria-label=\"Activity 4 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-4-d\">(d) UNTIL .................. Swap OR Last = 1 [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-4-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-4-d\" aria-label=\"Activity 4 part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-activity-4-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-activity-4-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478, May/June 2026 Paper 21, Question 4</p></div>"},{"id":"activity-5","label":"Extension: Sort the Other Way","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-activity-5","validatorKey":"y11l6_activity_5","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: Sort the Other Way</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This algorithm sorts a 2D array A in ascending order of column 2, swapping adjacent rows when they are the wrong way round.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">F &lt;- TRUE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">WHILE F DO</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;F &lt;- FALSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR I &lt;- 1 TO 9</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF A[I, 2] &gt; A[I + 1, 2]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;T1 &lt;- A[I, 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;T2 &lt;- A[I, 2]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A[I, 1] &lt;- A[I + 1, 1]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A[I, 2] &lt;- A[I + 1, 2]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A[I + 1, 1] &lt;- T1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A[I + 1, 2] &lt;- T2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;F &lt;- TRUE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT I</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDWHILE</div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-activity-5-a\">(a) Write the one line that must change so the same algorithm sorts A in descending order of column 2 instead. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-activity-5-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-5-a\" aria-label=\"Activity 5 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-activity-5-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 1 mark</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-activity-5-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><p class=\"exam-source\">Adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478, October/November 2025 Paper 22, Question 8</p></div>"},{"id":"formative","label":"Check Your Understanding","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check Your Understanding</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Questions to ask around the room:</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>What does a bubble sort compare on each step: every possible pair, or just neighbours?</li><li>What does the Swap flag being TRUE at the end of a pass tell you?</li><li>Why does the FOR loop run one fewer time than the number of items?</li><li>What is the largest number of full passes a bubble sort of 50 items could ever need?</li><li>How is the Swap flag here similar to the Found flag from linear search?</li></ul>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Sorted Already","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y11l6-plenary","validatorKey":"y11l6_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Sorted Already</h2><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-plenary-a\">(a) State what causes the WHILE NOT Swap loop to stop. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-plenary-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11l6-plenary-b\">(b) A list of 500 items is already fully sorted. State how many full passes this bubble sort needs before it stops. [1]</label><input id=\"y11l6-plenary-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11l6-plenary-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11l6-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"}],"validators":{"y11l6_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*1\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"ARRAY[1:50, ...] means indexing starts at 1, not 0 as in some other languages."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*50\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"The declaration ARRAY[1:50] runs from index 1 to index 50, so the last element is at index 50."}],"y11l6_activity_1":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*DECLARE\\s+Row\\s*:\\s*INTEGER\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Row is used to index the array and count through the loop, so it must be INTEGER, not STRING."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*Swap\\s*(<-|←)\\s*TRUE\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Each pass must assume it will find nothing out of order (Swap TRUE), so it can be proved wrong by an actual swap. Leaving it FALSE here means the WHILE NOT Swap loop can never end."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*FOR\\s+Row\\s*(<-|←)\\s*1\\s*TO\\s*199\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Starting at Row 2 skips ever comparing the first two names. The loop must start at 1."},{"suffix":"d","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*Names\\[\\s*Row\\s*,\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*(<-|←)\\s*Names\\[\\s*Row\\s*\\+\\s*1\\s*,\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"This line should move the first name (column 2) across, not overwrite the last name (column 1) that the previous line just set."},{"suffix":"e","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*NEXT\\s+Row\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The FOR loop's own control variable is Row, so it must close with NEXT Row - Column is never declared anywhere in this algorithm."}],"y11l6_activity_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*.{0,300}\\b(column\\s*1|first\\s*column|last\\s*name)\\b.{0,300}\\b(same|duplicate|multiple|identical|shared|more\\s*than\\s*one)\\b.{0,300}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The algorithm only compares the last name (column 1). Two people with the same last name are never sorted against each other by first name, so their relative order is whatever it happened to start as."}],"y11l6_activity_4":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*50\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Last tracks how far along the array still needs checking, and starts at the full length of Names[50]."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*FALSE\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Swap must be reset to FALSE at the start of every pass, so a pass with no swaps can be told apart from one with swaps."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*Index\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The rest of the algorithm already uses Index as the loop counter (Names[Index], Index + 1), so that is the variable the FOR line must declare."},{"suffix":"d","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*NOT\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"REPEAT...UNTIL keeps looping until its condition becomes true, so it must stop once NOT Swap OR Last = 1 - i.e. once a pass made no swaps, or only one item is left to check."}],"y11l6_activity_5":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*IF\\s+A\\[\\s*I\\s*,\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*<\\s*A\\[\\s*I\\s*\\+\\s*1\\s*,\\s*2\\s*\\]\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Swapping when the current value is smaller than the next pushes larger values towards the front instead of the back, sorting the array in descending order."}],"y11l6_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*.{0,200}\\b(no|zero|without|didn'?t\\s*need\\s*(any|a))\\b.{0,200}\\bswaps?\\b.{0,200}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The loop stops once a whole pass completes without a single swap - that is the algorithm's own proof that everything is already in order."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*1\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"A single pass across an already-sorted list makes no swaps, so Swap stays TRUE and the loop stops immediately after just one pass."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}